Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:01:32 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a8xx: use the A8xx compute workgroup tile height

Mesa reuses the A7xx WGTILEHEIGHT table on A8xx. Captures of the
Qualcomm driver on A840 instead show 16 / p, where p is the largest
power of two dividing local_size_y, capped at 16. The rule held for
all 44 captured dispatches, including different local sizes and
dispatch shapes, with and without shared memory and barriers.

Use the A8xx rule in Turnip, Gallium freedreno and computerator for
CHIP >= A8XX. Keep A7xx and older behavior unchanged.

Reported A840 compute shader replays at 1200 MHz show
up to 14.7% fewer GPU cycles per dispatch, with bit-identical outputs.
The 74,276-test Vulkan CTS selection (all compute, 10% subgroups and
10% memory_model) has identical results before and after the change.

